{
  "rule": "Content-anchored ratchet on hand-written except sqlite3 handlers that return a value in polylogue/. Each entry anchors one site as (file, sha1 of the normalized handler source); a count is present only where one file repeats literally identical handler text. Anchors may be removed, never added, and a handler whose text is not anchored here is a blocking finding. Anchors are deliberately not per-file counts: counts measured against two different bases sum on merge, so two separately green branches could redden master. Explicit failure-boundary rethrows are not census sites. Convert a seam to polylogue.core.evidence / polylogue.storage.tier_access and drop its anchors in the same change.",
